  {
    "sha": "96afea412eb6aa5f6c1559b39123c29dabab1bd3",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVVonwNoAKDk2YWZlYTQxMmViNmFhNWY2YzE1NTliMzkxMjNjMjlkYWJhYjFiZDM",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-20T11:39:01Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-20T11:39:01Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(ui): the shared report scrubs every path, on every system\n\nThe Report door's text leaves the machine. The first form replaced only\nthe project's own path in the status line; other status texts (for\nexample `open failed: <path>`) sent a full directory path. The shared\nreport now passes its whole text through report_scrub::scrub_paths:\neach path-like word (Windows drive and UNC, POSIX, `~`, relative forms,\neither separator, folder names with spaces) shrinks to its last\ncomponent. The status strip and the in-app Debug info do not change.\n\nfile_name_only now reads `/` and `\\` on every system, so a Windows\nmachine-file path in a project opened on Linux or macOS gives its file\nname too (Path::file_name sees no separator there).\n\nRefs #2744\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
      "tree": {
