  {
    "sha": "4fbd4922a041a29c14fc830b4965fd7185f3f526",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVVonwNoAKDRmYmQ0OTIyYTA0MWEyOWMxNGZjODMwYjQ5NjVmZDcxODVmM2Y1MjY",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-20T11:46:36Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-20T11:46:36Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(ui): a mark inside a folder name does not end a scrubbed path\n\nThe scrub stopped a path at a word that ends with `,` `;` `:` or a\nclosing mark. A folder such as `OneDrive - Contoso, Ltd` or\n`ACME (old) parts` thus sent the part of the name before the mark. A\npath now runs to the last later word of the line that has a separator;\na reason after the path (`<path>: access denied`) has none and stays.\nThe decision file states the rule and its known limits.\n\nRefs #2744\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
